invariant: INV-44
file: p384_wide_verify.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p384_wide_verify
reason: the host verifier admits n for r and for s, the first value
  past the range. n is zero modulo n, so the arithmetic after it gives
  the verdict zero gives, and every test passes. The proof requires
  the verdict 0 and no call into the points for a pair outside 1..n-1.

--- old
    return !p384_wide_is_zero(a) && p384_wide_compare(a, p384_wide_modn.m) < 0;
--- new
    return !p384_wide_is_zero(a) && p384_wide_compare(a, p384_wide_modn.m) <= 0;
